There are probably only a few items in NetHack that can properly be
classed as "useless".  The tin opener comes to mind, due to the
requirement to wield the damn thing.

By the same token, the majority of items in NetHack can also probably be
classed as "unnecessary".

> Would gems become more interesting if usable as slightly more damaging
> projectiles? Hardly (I suspect). To make damage, the priority is still
> the artifact weapons that you often ackquire even before you got your
> first hard gem.

I have dibbled with the idea of making slung gems shatter on impact
(_all_ gems, to avoid providing easy ID) for +dN damage, but
realistically, I'm not sure it will ever matter unless I make N be
something like "20" -- which is too far in the other direction.

The biggest problem WRT casual ranged combat right now appears to be:

- Max range isn't far enough to allow for "see monster, switch to ranged
  weapon, shoot at monster, switch to melee while he's one step away"
  unless you're only going to shoot at him once.

Increase max range, you say?  Great!  But when will it ever be useful?
Most rooms aren't that big, and the Mines sometimes have a straight line
long enough, but not that often.  No real help there.

I'm seriously considering having a "missile launcher slot" for your
player to automatically switch to, much like a)pplying a polearm
automatically wields it.  (You'd have to unwield it manually.)  This
doesn't sound like much but if it removes a tiny bit of tedium WRT using
ranged launchers, perhaps it would be good.

